<!-- Scholarships Section -->
<section class="card" id="scholarships">
  <h2>About Scholarships</h2>
  <p>Students of our institute are eligible for the following major scholarship schemes:</p>

  <h3>1. SVMCM (Swami Vivekananda Merit-cum-Means Scholarship)</h3>
  <p>
    Offered by the Government of West Bengal for meritorious students based on academic performance. Students must score at least 60% in the previous examination to be eligible.
    Link: <a href="https://svmcm.wb.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">svmcm.wb.gov.in</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The scholarship amount provided by the Directorate of Technical Education and Training (DTE&amp;T) for students enrolled in Polytechnic Colleges/Institutions is ₹18,000 per annum.
  </p>
  <p><strong>List of Documents Required for Submission at the College:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Duly filled Application Form</li>
    <li>Marksheet of Madhyamik Examination or its equivalent</li>
    <li>Marksheet of the most recent board examination</li>
    <li>Admission Receipt</li>
    <li>Income Certificate</li>
    <li>Domicile Proof – Aadhaar / Voter ID / Ration Card / Certificate by competent authority</li>
    <li>Photocopy of Bank Passbook (first page showing name and account details)</li>
    <li>Year Gap Certificate (if applicable)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2. OASIS (For SC/ST/OBC Students)</h3>
  <p>
    A state government scholarship dedicated to students from Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes, and OBC communities.
    Link: <a href="https://oasis.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">oasis.gov.in</a>.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Required Documents:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Stamp-size colour photo (attested)</li>
    <li>Attested copy of last exam marksheet/certificate</li>
    <li>Copy of first page of bank passbook</li>
    <li>Income certificate & proof of DOB (Birth Certificate / Madhyamik Admit Card)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. Aikyashree (For Minority Students)</h3>
  <p>
    Managed by the West Bengal Minorities Development & Finance Corporation, this scholarship supports students from minority communities.
    Link: <a href="https://wbmdfcscholarship.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">wbmdfcscholarship.in</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>4. NSP (National Scholarship Portal)</h3>
  <p>
    A central government scholarship platform hosting various schemes from different ministries and state governments.
    Apply at <a href="https://scholarships.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">scholarships.gov.in</a>.
  </p>
</section>


